   "text": "I read the drawing as a macrocyclic peptide-like ring and wrote the SMILES from its parts.\n\n- **Ornithine residue:** H2N\u2011(CH2)3\u2011CH with its alpha\u2011NH bonded to a CH2 on pyridine C3. Its C=O links to the lysine NH.\n- **Lysine residue:** NH\u2011CH with a (CH2)4NH2 side chain. Its C=O links to the N\u2011methyl nitrogen of tryptophan.\n- **N\u2011methyl tryptophan residue:** N(CH3)\u2011CH(CH2\u2011indol\u20113\u2011yl)\u2011C(=O). Its C=O links to an NH that carries a CH2 on the central benzene ring.\n- **Central benzene ring, substituents in order around the ring:** CH2NH, then 4\u2011carboxyphenyl, then two ring CH, then OCH3, then S. The S is bonded to pyridine C2, which closes the macrocycle.\n\nFor stereochemistry, I assumed all three stereocentres are L (S), consistent with the wedge bonds drawn. I did not check each wedge against the CIP rules. I worked out the chirality symbols from the atom order in the SMILES: the ornithine centre needs `@` and the lysine and tryptophan centres need `@@`.\n\nSMILES: NCCC[C@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)C(=O)NCc2c(ccc(OC)c2Sc2ncccc2CN1)-c1ccc(C(=O)O)cc1"
